sequenceDiagram
    actor User as CLI User
    participant RC as RunCommand<br/>(implements JobLaunch.Listener)
    participant JL as JobLaunch
    participant JS as JobSession
    participant Port as RunAws port<br/>(AwsRunAws in production)
    participant S3 as AWS S3
    participant SSM as AWS SSM
    participant EC2 as AWS EC2
    participant CF as AWS CloudFormation
    participant DDB as DynamoDB results table
    participant GH as GitHub Releases (laptop only)

    User->>RC: baas run <type> [params] --benchmark-jar <path> [--project] [--instance-type] [--timeout]<br/>[--watchdog-margin] [--runner-jar] [--jdk id] [--tag k=v] [--format json] [--detach]
    Note over RC: execute() -- before any AWS call:<br/>--format text or json, else exit 2. type in BenchmarkType.commandNames(), else exit 2.<br/>An unreleased CLI (BaasVersion.isReleased() false) without --runner-jar -> exit 1. baas run builds nothing.
    RC->>RC: OperatorSession.of(Invocation.configService(spec)).config()
    Note over RC: resolveProject -- --project, or GitProject.repositoryName of the JAR's directory<br/>when git.resolveProject is on, else IllegalStateException naming --project.<br/>resolveResultsTable, instanceType, resolveTimings -> watchdogBound = timeout + margin (margin >= 60).<br/>buildRunnerTags: project, type, source + every --tag. A machine-observed key or project is REJECTED.<br/>--benchmark-jar missing on disk -> exit 1.
    RC->>JL: new JobLaunch(awsFactory.apply(operatorSession.factory()), config.names(), this).run(Request)

    JL->>Port: currentImage(/<prefix>/runner/ami-id)
    Port->>SSM: getParameter (ImageBuilderService.currentImage)
    Port->>EC2: describeImages(amiId) -- baas-image-version and baas-jdks tags
    alt no pointer or no image
        JL-->>RC: noImageMessage (names admin image build), 1 -- nothing uploaded
    end
    Note over JL: selectJdk -- --jdk, else the image's default (first in baas-jdks).<br/>An id the tag does not name -> exit 2 listing the ids. An image without baas-jdks<br/>refuses any --jdk (exit 2, names admin image build) and runs without one, on java from PATH.
    JL->>Port: stackOutputs(<prefix>)
    Port->>CF: describeStacks -- SubnetId, SecurityGroupId
    Note over JL: resolveNetworking: a missing output throws, before any upload
    Note over JL: ONE clock read: jobInstant = Instant.now()<br/>jobId = JobId.generate(jobInstant), resultPath = JobLayout.jobPrefix(project, jobId)
    JL->>RC: Listener.named(jobId, resultPath)
    JL->>Port: upload(benchmark JAR, JobLayout.benchmarkJarKey)
    Port->>S3: putObject jobs/<project>/<jobId>/input/benchmark.jar
    alt --runner-jar given
        JL->>Port: upload(runner JAR, JobLayout.runnerJarOverrideKey)
        Port->>S3: putObject jobs/<project>/<jobId>/input/runner.jar
    else pinned to this CLI's version
        JL->>Port: pinnedRunnerJar(bucket, version, sourceRepo)
        Port->>S3: RunnerJarResolver.resolve -- head releases/<version>/benchmark-runner.jar
        opt absent
            Port->>GH: fetch benchmark-runner.jar + .sha256
            Note over Port: verify -- a mismatch throws, nothing launched
            Port->>S3: putObject If-None-Match * (412/409 = another launch seeded it)
        end
    end
    Note over JL: new UserDataScriptBuilder().build(...) with job.sortKey() from ResultKeys and JDK_ID --<br/>installs nothing. The runner gets --jdk, which starts the benchmark on /opt/jdks/id/bin/java
    JL->>JS: new JobSession(job, recorder, stopRecorder (5 s client), instances)
    JL->>JS: reserve()
    JS->>DDB: UpdateItem status launching + identity, condition attribute_not_exists(pk)
    alt reservation fails
        JL-->>RC: 1 -- NOTHING is launched
    end
    JL->>RC: Listener.reserved(session)
    Note over RC: shutdownHooks.accept(new Thread(onShutdown)) -- armed BEFORE RunInstances:<br/>on any JVM exit, a session not ended and not detached gets stop(cancelled)
    JL->>Port: instances.runInstance(ami, type, subnet, sg, profile, userData, jobId, prefix)
    Port->>EC2: RunInstances -- Ec2ProvisioningService: clientToken = jobId, IMDSv2 required,<br/>tags only project=baas, baas-role, baas-job-id, baas-deployment
    alt RunInstances throws
        JL->>JS: recordLaunchFailed(errorCode)
        JS->>DDB: UpdateItem launch-failed + errorCode, never over a terminal status (best effort)
        JL->>Port: putText(JobLayout.launchErrorKey) -- launch-error.txt (best effort)
        JL-->>RC: 1
    end
    EC2-->>JL: instanceId
    JL->>RC: Listener.launched(instanceId)
    JL->>JS: confirmLaunched(instanceId)
    JS->>DDB: UpdateItem launched + instanceId, only while status = launching
    Note over JS: WRITTEN -> CONFIRMED. Write failed -> UNCONFIRMED (the instance records itself).<br/>REFUSED -> strong re-read: endsItself or running -> CONFIRMED,<br/>another terminal status (cancelled) -> terminate the instance, CANCELLED_WHILE_LAUNCHING
    alt CANCELLED_WHILE_LAUNCHING
        JL-->>RC: 1
    else --detach (ADR 0007)
        JL->>RC: Listener.detached(launched, or launching if unconfirmed)
        Note over RC: detached = true -- from here onShutdown leaves the job alone.<br/>The instance ends the job itself. Follow it: jobs show. Stop it: jobs terminate.
        JL-->>RC: 0 -- NO poll
    end

    JL->>RC: Listener.openStatusLine() -- null under --format json (log lines instead)
    loop JobSession.await, every 15 s
        JS->>DDB: GetItem ConsistentRead
        alt terminal status stored
            Note over JS: finish -- a cancelled written elsewhere also terminates a live instance.<br/>completed, failed:N, timed-out (the watchdog's) are left to end themselves.
        else instance terminated or shutting-down
            JS->>DDB: re-read once
            Note over JS: still no terminal status -> measurements stored (Port.jobRows) ?<br/>status-lost : vanished -- both exit 1
        else elapsed > watchdog bound (the poll cap)
            JS->>DDB: one last read, then stop(timed-out) -- JobStop: write under 5 s, then terminate
        else still going
            JS->>EC2: describeInstances(instanceId) -- state
            JS->>JL: progress(state, elapsed)
            JL-->>User: StatusLine.update on STDOUT when interactive, else "Still running (state)... elapsed" on stderr
        end
    end
    alt completed, and -lprof was the only argument after --
        JL->>Port: getText(bucket, jobPrefix/jmh-output.txt)
        Port->>S3: GetObject -- the listing the runner uploaded, no measurements read
        JL->>RC: Listener.printListing(listing, jobId)
        RC-->>User: the listing verbatim on stdout (with --format json only a log line)
    else completed
        JL->>Port: jobRows(table, jobId)
        Port->>DDB: ResultsQueryService.queryByJobId -- jobId-index, attribute_exists(kind), no hidden filter
        JL->>RC: Listener.printResults(rows, jobId)
        RC-->>User: ResultsTable on stdout (with --format json only a log line)
    else failed:N, timed-out, cancelled, vanished, status-lost
        JL-->>RC: logs the runner log path -- exit 1
    end
    JL-->>RC: exit code
    opt --format json -- in call()'s finally, on the failure path too
        RC-->>User: printJobSummary -- {jobId, project, resultPath, status, jobStatus, exitCode, instanceId}
    end
    Note over RC,User: hints (interactive only): detached -> jobs show / jobs terminate,<br/>completed -> query --job-id / jobs download,<br/>a completed -lprof listing -> jobs download alone, otherwise -> jobs show / jobs download
